# blocks.pdl - what can be mined / destroyed and what it leaves behind (owner 2026-10-25). Re-read every 2 s.
# Design: BOOK 16.game/RPG-SPACE-COLLISION-AND-DESTRUCTION-DESIGN.md sections 3, 4c, 4g. Fun first; the extra columns are kept for a realistic ruleset (nothing reads them yet).
# BLOCK | kind | hardness | drops | count | damaged_pct | composition | density | melting_point
# hardness = mining power needed in total (tool power is added per mine action); damaged_pct = chance (0..100) that a remnant is damaged.
BLOCK | rock     | 3  | stone | 2 | 10 | SiO2   | 2.6 | 1700
